# Actual v1 migration fixture

`v1-datadir.tar.gz` is a physical RocksDB datadir produced by the unchanged
predecessor Rust lineage 2 executable in this maintenance workspace. It contains
one terminal receipt, three durably admitted pending jobs, and a cancellation
intent on sequence 3. The process was killed only after admission/cancellation
acknowledgments. No rows were manufactured for this fixture.

`v1-manifest.json` records SHA-256 hashes of the producing executable, archive,
and every logical row. The capture script opens its independent inspector only
after the writer has exited. Fixture extraction and migration use a fresh copy;
the archive is never opened as a live database.

The normal test suite consumes this saved archive. To reproduce a capture with
the preserved predecessor executable, use the broker:

```sh
python3 run.py 'python3 tests/make_v1_fixture.py /workspace/tmp/pre-maintenance/service-v1' 120
```

Do not regenerate with the upgraded executable: the purpose is to prove actual
v1-to-v2 recovery. The script requires receipt/pending/cancel preconditions and
fails if work terminalizes before capture; it does not silently retry.
